{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.branch_trace_character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.branch_trace_character","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L131-L140","doc":"**Corollary (the case used downstream).** Taking `β₁ = β₂ = Iid`\n(the algebra identity) recovers the scalar form\n`χ^λ(I) = Σ_{μ,ν} tr A^λ_{μ,ν}(I)` consumed by the operator-valued\nFrobenius budget (`rem:operator-valued-magnitude-budget`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.branch_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.branch_trace","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L108-L129","doc":"**Branching trace decomposition** (`prop:hecke-branching-trace-decomposition`),\nconditional on the class per §3b-cond.  For any `λ` and any interface\nelement `I` with braid factors `β₁, β₂`, the interface trace decomposes\nas the sum of the operator-valued block traces over `(μ ⊢ n, ν ⊢ m)`.\n\n**Derived, not assumed.** The proof is: rewrite both sides into the branched\nbasis by H2 and H3, then split a sum over `Σ p, Fin (blockDim p)` into a sum\nover blocks of sums within blocks. No hypothesis about the operator is used\n— a trace reads only the diagonal, so block-diagonality is not needed\neither. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:hecke-branching-trace-decomposition","label":"prop:hecke-branching-trace-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockTrace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockTrace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L101-L101","doc":"**H3 — the block trace is the diagonal sum over that block.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.interfaceTrace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.interfaceTrace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L97-L97","doc":"**H2 — the interface trace is that matrix's trace.** Trace is\nbasis-independent, so this identifies the named scalar with the branched\npicture. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockTrace","kind":"def","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Per-block summand `tr_{V_μ⊗V_ν}(A^λ_{μ,ν}(I)·(ρ_μ(β₁)⊗ρ_ν(β₂)))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.interfaceTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.interfaceTrace","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Left-hand side: `tr_{V_λ}(ρ_λ(β₁ · I · β₂))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.branchedMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.branchedMatrix","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L87-L87","doc":"**H1 — the branching.** The matrix of `ρ_λ(β₁ · I · β₂)` in a basis\nindexed by `(block, position within block)`. Its existence *is* the\nbranching rule; nothing here derives it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockDim","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L83-L83","doc":"`dim (V_μ ⊗ V_ν)` for the block `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockFintype","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockFintype","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L81-L81","doc":"Each block index set is finite (finitely many partitions). Declared as an\ninstance binder so the sigma-indexed matrix type below elaborates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.blockIndex","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L78-L78","doc":"The finite set of `(μ ⊢ n, ν ⊢ m)` block indices feeding `λ`,\nwith Littlewood–Richardson multiplicities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.HeckeBranchingTraceDecomposition","kind":"class","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/hecke-branching-trace-decomposition.lean#L55-L104","doc":"Abstract carrier data for the Hecke branching trace decomposition at\nparameter `q`.\n\nBecause Mathlib lacks the Hoefsmit seminormal basis and the\nHecke-character infrastructure, the branched representation is modelled\nabstractly:\n\n* `blockIndex lam` is the finite index set of `(μ ⊢ n, ν ⊢ m)` pairs\n  contributing to `λ`, carrying the Littlewood–Richardson multiplicities\n  `c^λ_{μν}` (a pair occurring with multiplicity `c` appears `c` times);\n* `blockDim lam p` is `dim (V_μ ⊗ V_ν)` for that block;\n* `branchedMatrix lam I β₁ β₂` is the matrix of `ρ_λ(β₁ · I · β₂)` in the\n  branched basis, indexed by `(block, position within block)`;\n* `interfaceTrace` and `blockTrace` are the named scalars of the\n  proposition, tied to that matrix by `interfaceTrace_eq` / `blockTrace_eq`.\n\nThe conjectural content is the branching itself — that such a basis exists\nand that the named scalars are read off it. The **sum rule is not a field**:\nit is derived in `branch_trace`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}